# MESSAGE: extraction query example. One row per compat:Widget, with the
# MESSAGE: ordered multi-valued field (widgetTagItem) GROUP_CONCAT-joined in
# MESSAGE: deterministic order. Each list item is its own compat:ListItem
# MESSAGE: blank node (itemText + itemOrder) -- NOT a flat value/order
# MESSAGE: property pair directly on the Widget subject. See ontology.ttl.example
# MESSAGE: for why the flat shape corrupts GROUP_CONCAT with a cartesian
# MESSAGE: product (found and fixed live in story-pack's first draft).
# MESSAGE:
# MESSAGE: The pattern that avoids the bug has two required parts, both
# MESSAGE: present below:
# MESSAGE:   1. ORDER BY ?ord INSIDE the inner SELECT, before aggregation.
# MESSAGE:      GROUP_CONCAT alone does not guarantee row order; SPARQL 1.1
# MESSAGE:      only guarantees order if an ORDER BY is evaluated on the
# MESSAGE:      solution sequence feeding the aggregate.
# MESSAGE:   2. A subselect (OPTIONAL { SELECT ... (GROUP_CONCAT(...) AS ?x)
# MESSAGE:      WHERE { SELECT ... } GROUP BY ?entity }) rather than grouping
# MESSAGE:      in the outer WHERE directly -- this keeps each multi-valued
# MESSAGE:      field's join independent, so adding a second ordered property
# MESSAGE:      later doesn't reintroduce a cross-multiplication between the
# MESSAGE:      two unrelated lists.
# MESSAGE:
# MESSAGE: Separator is "%%WIDGET_SEP%%", not a bare "|" or ",": real item
# MESSAGE: text may legitimately contain both (same reasoning as
# MESSAGE: story-pack's "%%STORY_SEP%%" and github-actions-pack's
# MESSAGE: workflow.yml.tmpl).
PREFIX compat: <https://chatmangpt.com/ns/wasm4pm/compat#>
SELECT ?widget ?widgetId ?widgetName ?widgetTags
WHERE {
  ?widget a compat:Widget ;
          compat:widgetId ?widgetId ;
          compat:widgetName ?widgetName .

  OPTIONAL {
    SELECT ?widget (GROUP_CONCAT(?text; separator="%%WIDGET_SEP%%") AS ?widgetTags) WHERE {
      SELECT ?widget ?text WHERE {
        ?widget compat:widgetTagItem ?item .
        ?item compat:itemText ?text ; compat:itemOrder ?ord .
      } ORDER BY ?ord
    } GROUP BY ?widget
  }
}
ORDER BY ?widgetId
